in A Song of Ice and Fire award is  described as someone who can enter the  mind of a wolf less specific terms would  be be sling or skin-changer these terms  refer to someone who can enter the mind  of animals and do their bidding through  them the ability to skin change is well  known amongst the free folk beyond the  wall and the power set to go back  thousands of years in our story it is  known that all the star children have  the ability to skin change according to  Vera mere six skins of the free folk  skin changes can sense each other and  know immediately whether or not they are  in the presence of one with the gift  upon seeing Jon Snow  bear Amir immediately recognizes Jon's  ability as a wall suggesting even that  Jon may be even more powerful than their  Amir himself Arya Stark unlike Jon Snow  has demonstrated herself to be more than  simply award during her training of the  faceless men Arya Stark is blinded as a  punishment for the killing of Darion the  singer it is in this moment that her  gift as a skin-changer truly activates  she uses her power to see through the  eyes of stray cat even though she does  not realize that she is doing it Arya  also transfers her consciousness to her  dire wolf Nymeria when she sleeps  although she believed that what she sees  are merely dreams bran stark it's  certainly the most powerful not least  our children he has a gift of skin  changing it's so powerful and he can  transfer his mind even into human hosts  a task in which they ultra powerful very  mere six skins  feyo's act in addition to being a very  powerful skin ginger bran is also a  green seer he has the ability to reach  through the veil of time and see beyond  the little is known of the extent of it  Rickon Stark seems possessed some  greenseer ability as well after Ned is  killed he and his brother bran both  dream of their father dead inside the  crypts of Winterfell  father is not here yes he is I saw him  tears glistened on written faith I saw  him last night  in your dream Rickon nodded you leave  him you leave him be he's coming home  now like he promised he's coming home  less is known to what extent Sansa and  Robb Stark possess these abilities as  well but it has been confirmed by author  george RR martin that all the stark  children indeed do possess some  skin-changer ability why is the ability  to skin change so prevalent amongst the  stark children the obvious answer is  genetics the Starks have wild in blood  and as I mentioned earlier skin changing  is a well-known gift beyond the wall but  even the wildlings weren't the first to  possess these abilities the first skin  changers and green seers were the  children of the forest it is said that  during the hundreds of years of conflict  between the children of the forest and  men lacking in physical strength and  sophisticated weaponry  the children would used their power to  employ animals to fight for them the  wise men of the children were called  green seers they too had the power to  see beyond so what the children of the  forest were the original users of the  power and how did mankind come to  possess it well it may be possible that  the children of the forest taught these  abilities to mankind but if that was the  case then why does it now appear to be  genetic I think the more likely answer  must be that the children did not teach  these gifts to men they simply bred with  men passing down these abilities the  Starks are one of the oldest houses in  Westeros descended from the first men if  the blood of the children may exist in  any bloodline then the Starks would be  the perfect candidate but there is  another mystery to be answered if the  skin-changer ability is genetic then why  is it that no other Starks are mentioned  to have this ability  if this gift was truly in the start  bloodline would it not have manifested  in many Starks throughout the centuries  why is there no evidence of other Starks  with these powers perhaps it is because  these Starks have something that few  others have had  real dire roles upon discovering the  wolves in a game of groans the group is  confused as to why the animals are there  for dire wolves haven't been seen south  of the wall in thousands of years in  regards to the animals that the children  of the forest used to fight for them  dire wolves are mentioned very first in  the world of Ice and Fire  the term warg itself is the only term in  the books that refers to a specific  animal being skinned changed a wolf is  there something inherently special about  the dire wolves that awakens a latent  skin-changer ability upon discovery of  the first five wolves Jon Snow  inexplicably turns back to find a sixth  war which has separated away from the  other five almost as if he could already  sense its presence but there are other  beasts mentioned specifically that the  children had control over snow bears and  mammoths which are found only north of  the wall lions which were hunted to  extinction by the first men serpents  which could never survive in the north  of Westeros due to the cold and eagles  these animals are all either extinct or  out of reach for most Starks born after  the raising of the wall if it requires  one of these animal familiars of sorts  to awaken skin-changer abilities then it  seems to explain why there are no other  Starks that have demonstrated these  gifts and it also seems important to  note that each of the Starks were  children at the point where they came  into contact with their dire wolves for  the first time the oldest being Robb  Stark at age 14  the stark magic seems to be latent  genetic ability present within the stark  bloodline that was awakened by the  presence of these dire wolves knowing  that a Song of Ice and Fire is rarely  ever what it appears to be on the  surface it is hard to accept that these  dire wolves showing up when they did was  a coincidence  perhaps they were sent by bloodraven who  saw the necessity of it in his grand  scheme or perhaps even stranger more  powerful forces were behind the  appearance of these wolves  the answer is unclear but what is clear  is that the start children each possess  power of their own that once honed could  be used in ways that no one has foreseen  [Music]
 

